   "he": "עַד יָמָיו הָיָה פַּטִּישׁ מַכֶּה בִּירוּשָׁלַיִם. בְּחוּלּוֹ שֶׁל מוֹעֵד.",
   "en": "The mishna stated that «until the days» of Yoḥanan the High Priest «the hammer» of smiths «would strike in Jerusalem.» The Gemara explains: This is referring «to the intermediate days of a Festival.» Though certain types of labor are permitted on those days, the banging of a hammer was outlawed, as the noise it made would detract from the feeling of sanctity of the day."
  }
